data/
# The working config library: this installation's own engines, missions, vehicles, studies and
# sizing coefficients. Deliberately untracked -- it is operator data, not source, and much of it
# is under agreements that do not travel with the code. Seed it by copying examples/configs
# (see the README); the tracked template lives there.
#
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored `configs/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which silently swallows examples/configs -- the template that has to
# ship -- and the only symptom is a recipient with nothing to copy.
/configs/
# `runs/` is anchored for the same reason: examples/runs ships a finished sweep.
# And the singular spelling. A config library named `config/` is the same operator data
# under a different name, and it has been committed by accident once already.
/config/
*.bsp
*.bsp.win
.ruff_cache/
# Licensed MONTE build artifacts + ephemeris data. The image is built outside this repository
# from a distribution that cannot be committed alongside it; these patterns keep a local build
# from ever landing here if somebody stages one in-tree.
docker/
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
coverage.xml
.coverage
